{
  "dom_id": "step-q79648",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Find the greatest common divisor of $975$ and $221.$",
  "worked_solution": "We use the Euclidean algorithm, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}975 & = & 221(4) & + & 91 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 221 & = & 91(2) & + & 39 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 91 & = & 39(2) & + & 13 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 39 & = & 13(3) & + & 0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe last positive remainder is $13.$ Therefore, we conclude that the greatest common divisor of $975$ and $221$ is $13.$ Symbolically, we write\n\n$$\n\\text{gcd}(975,221)=13.\n$$",
